lass="programlisting"><div class="codeinput"><pre>rng(<span style="color:#A020F0">'default'</span>) <span style="color:#228B22">% For reproducibility</span>
rv = normrnd(0,1,1000,5);</pre></div></div></div><p>Find the range values of the samples.</p><div class="code_responsive"><div class="programlisting"><div class="codeinput"><pre>near6 = range(rv)</pre></div></div></div><div class="code_responsive"><div class="programlisting"><div class="codeoutput"><pre>near6 = <span class="emphasis"><em>1×5</em></span>

    6.8104    6.6420    6.9578    6.0860    6.8165

</pre></div></div></div><p>The range value is approximately 6 for each sample.</p><div class="procedure"></div></div></div></div></div><div itemscope="" itemtype="http://www.mathworks.com/help/schema/MathWorksDocPage/Example" itemprop="example" class="em_example"><meta itemprop="exampleid" content="stats-ex78196306"></meta><meta itemprop="exampletitle" content="Range of Standard Normal Random Numbers"></meta></div><div class="panel-group" role="tablist" aria-multiselectable="true" id="expand_panel_heading_mw_9cefe705-3154-47c7-a69c-75fe5b4660b5"><div class="panel panel-default "><div role="tab" data-toggle="collapse" id="expand_panel_heading_mw_9cefe705-3154-47c7-a69c-75fe5b4660b5" data-target="#expand_panel_body_mw_9cefe705-3154-47c7-a69c-75fe5b4660b5" aria-controls="expand_panel_body_mw_9cefe705-3154-47c7-a69c-75fe5b4660b5" class="panel-heading add_cursor_pointer" aria-expanded="true"><h3 class="panel-title" id="mw_9cefe705-3154-47c7-a69c-75fe5b4660b5">Range of Exam Scores<br/> </h3><span class="icon-arrow-open-down icon_24"></span><span class="icon-arrow-open-right icon_24"></span></div><div role="tabpanel" id="expand_panel_body_mw_9cefe705-3154-47c7-a69c-75fe5b4660b5" aria-labelledby="expand_panel_heading_mw_9cefe705-3154-47c7-a69c-75fe5b4660b5" class="panel-collapse collapse in"><div class="panel-body"><div class="pull-right examples_short_list" style="width:250px; margin-left: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px;"><div data-pane="metadata" style="margin-bottom: 0px;" class="panel metadata_container"><div class="panel-body metadata_content" style="padding-top:0px; padding-bottom:0px;"><div class="row"><div class="col-xs-12"><a class="btn btn_secondary btn-block" href="matlab:openExample('stats/RangeOfExamScoresExample')">Open Live Script</a></div></div></div></div></div><p class="shortdesc">Find the range of exam scores over the course of five exams.</p><p>Load the <code class="literal">examgrades</code> data set.</p><div class="code_responsive"><div class="programlisting"><div class="codeinput"><pre>load <span style="color:#A020F0">examgrades</span></pre></div></div></div><p>Find the range of all exam scores.</p><div class="code_responsive"><div class="programlisting"><div class="codeinput"><pre>y = range(grades,<span style="color:#A020F0">'all'</span>)</pre></div></div></div><div class="code_responsive"><div class="programlisting"><div class="codeoutput"><pre>y = 46
</pre></div></div></div><div class="procedure"></div></div></div></div></div><div itemscope="" itemtype="http://www.mathworks.com/help/schema/MathWorksDocPage/Example" itemprop="example" class="em_example"><meta itemprop="exampleid" content="stats-ex39126168"></meta><meta itemprop="exampletitle" content="Range of Exam Scores"></meta></div><div class="panel-group" role="tablist" aria-multiselectable="true" id="expand_panel_heading_mw_40e11744-5dbe-443b-b017-8c8394439f43"><div class="panel panel-default "><div role="tab" data-toggle="collapse" id="expand_panel_heading_mw_40e11744-5dbe-443b-b017-8c8394439f43" data-target="#expand_panel_body_mw_40e11744-5dbe-443b-b017-8c8394439f43" aria-controls="expand_panel_body_mw_40e11744-5dbe-443b-b017-8c8394439f43" class="panel-heading add_cursor_pointer" aria-expanded="true"><h3 class="panel-title" id="mw_40e11744-5dbe-443b-b017-8c8394439f43">Range of Exam Scores by Student<br/> </h3><span class="icon-arrow-open-down icon_24"></span><span class="icon-arrow-open-right icon_24"></span></div><div role="tabpanel" id="expand_panel_body_mw_40e11744-5dbe-443b-b017-8c8394439f43" aria-labelledby="expand_panel_heading_mw_40e11744-5dbe-443b-b017-8c8394439f43" class="panel-collapse collapse in"><div class="panel-body"><div class="pull-right examples_short_list" style="width:250px; margin-left: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px;"><div data-pane="metadata" style="margin-bottom: 0px;" class="panel metadata_container"><div class="panel-body metadata_content" style="padding-top:0px; padding-bottom:0px;"><div class="row"><div class="col-xs-12"><a class="btn btn_secondary btn-block" href="matlab:openExample('stats/RangeOfExamScoresByStudentExample')">Open Live Script</a></div></div></div></div></div><p class="shortdesc">Find the range of exam scores for each student over the course of five exams.</p><p>Load the <code class="literal">examgrades</code> data set.</p><div class="code_responsive"><div class="programlisting"><div class="codeinput"><pre>load <span style="color:#A020F0">examgrades</span></pre></div></div></div><p>Find the range of exam scores for the first 10 students.  For example, the difference between the eighth student's best and worst exam scores is 7 points.</p><div class="code_responsive"><div class="programlisting"><div class="codeinput"><pre>X = grades(1:10,:);
y = range(X,2)</pre></div></div></div><div class="code_responsive"><div class="programlisting"><div class="codeoutput"><pre>y = <span class="emphasis"><em>10×1</em></span>

    12
    13
    10
    12
     8
    16
    14
     7
    12
    10

</pre></div></div></div><div class="procedure"></div></div></div></div></div><div itemscope="" itemtype="http://www.mathworks.com/help/schema/MathWorksDocPage/Example" itemprop="example" class="em_example"><meta itemprop="exampleid" content="stats-ex78797827"></meta><meta itemprop="exampletitle" content="Range of Exam Scores by Student"></meta></div><div class="panel-group" role="tablist" aria-multiselectable="true" id="expand_panel_heading_mw_939ea76d-e4a5-4d6b-b786-f458da49d025"><div class="panel panel-default "><div role="tab" data-toggle="collapse" id="expand_panel_heading_mw_939ea76d-e4a5-4d6b-b786-f458da49d025" data-target="#expand_panel_body_mw_939ea76d-e4a5-4d6b-b786-f458da49d025" aria-controls="expand_panel_body_mw_939ea76d-e4a5-4d6b-b786-f458da49d025" class="panel-heading add_cursor_pointer" aria-expanded="true"><h3 class="panel-title" id="mw_939ea76d-e4a5-4d6b-b786-f458da49d025">Range Along Vector Dimension<br/> </h3><span class="icon-arrow-open-down icon_24"></span><span class="icon-arrow-open-right icon_24"></span></div><div role="tabpanel" id="expand_panel_body_mw_939ea76d-e4a5-4d6b-b786-f458da49d025" aria-labelledby="expand_panel_heading_mw_939ea76d-e4a5-4d6b-b786-f458da49d025" class="panel-collapse collapse in"><div class="panel-body"><div class="pull-right examples_short_list" style="width:250px; margin-left: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px;"><div data-pane="metadata" style="margin-bottom: 0px;" class="panel metadata_container"><div class="panel-body metadata_content" style="padding-top:0px; padding-bottom:0px;"><div class="row"><div class="col-xs-12"><a class="btn btn_secondary btn-block" href="matlab:openExample('stats/RangeOfMultidimensionalArrayExample')">Open Live Script</a></div></div></div></div></div><p class="shortdesc">Find the range of a multidimensional array over multiple dimensions.</p><p>Create a 3-by-5-by-2 array of normal random numbers with mean <code class="literal">mu = 2</code> and standard deviation <code class="literal">sigma = 7</code>.</p><div class="code_responsive"><div class="programlisting"><div class="codeinput"><pre>rng(<span style="color:#A020F0">'default'</span>) <span style="color:#228B22">% For reproducibility</span>
mu = 2;
sigma = 7;
X = normrnd(mu,sigma,[3 5 2])</pre></div></div></div><div class="code_responsive"><div class="programlisting"><div class="codeoutput"><pre>X = 
X(:,:,1) =

    5.7637    8.0352   -1.0351   21.3861    7.0778
   14.8372    4.2314    4.3984   -7.4492    1.5586
  -13.8119   -7.1538   27.0488   23.2445    7.0032


X(:,:,2) =

    0.5652   11.8632   -6.4524    5.4223   -0.1241
    1.1310   11.9203    7.0207    9.2429    4.0571
   12.4279    6.7005   13.4116    7.0882   -3.5110

</pre></div></div></div><p>Find the range of each page of <code class="literal">X</code> by specifying dimensions 1 and 2 as the operating dimensions.</p><div class="code_responsive"><div class="programlisting"><div class="codeinput"><pre>ypage = range(X,[1 2])</pre></div></div></div><div class="code_responsive"><div class="programlisting"><div class="codeoutput"><pre>ypage = 
ypage(:,:,1) =

   40.8607


ypage(:,:,2) =

   19.8641

</pre></div></div></div><p>For example, <code class="literal">ypage(1,1,2)</code> is the range of all the elements in <code class="literal">X(:,:,2)</code>.</p><p>Find the range of the elements in each <code class="literal">X(i,:,:)</code> slice by specifying dimensions 2 and 3 as the operating dimensions.</p><div class="code_responsive"><div class="programlisting"><div class="codeinput"><pre>yrow = range(X,[2 3])</pre></div></div></div><div class="code_responsive"><div class="programlisting"><div class="codeoutput"><pre>yrow = <span class="emphasis"><em>3×1</em></span>

   27.8385
   22.2864
   40.8607

</pre></div></div></div><p>For example, <code class="literal">yrow(3)</code> is the range of all the elements in <code class="literal">X(3,:,:)</code>.</p><div class="procedure"></div></div></div></div></div><div itemscope="" itemtype="http://www.mathworks.com/help/schema/MathWorksDocPage/Example" itemprop="example" class="em_example"><meta itemprop="exampleid" content="stats-ex21584899"></meta><meta itemprop="exampletitle" content="Range Along Vector Dimension"></meta></div></div></div><div class="ref_sect"><h2 id="d120e631068">Input Arguments</h2><div class="expandableContent"><p class="switch "><a href="javascript:void(0);" class="expandAllLink" data-allexpanded="true">collapse all</a></p><div class="panel-group" id="d120e631068_panel-group" role="tablist" aria-multiselectable="true"><div class="panel-group" role="tablist" aria-multiselectable="true"><div class="panel panel-default "><div itemscope="" itemprop="inputargument" itemtype="http://www.mathworks.com/help/schema/MathWorksDocPage/NamedInputArgument" itemid="d120e631073"><div role="tab" data-toggle="collapse" id="expand_panel_heading_d120e631073" data-target="#expand_panel_body_d120e631073" aria-controls="expand_panel_body_d120e631073" class="panel-heading add_cursor_pointer" aria-expanded="true"><span id="inputarg_X" class="anchor_target"></span><h3 class="panel-title" id="d120e631073"><code itemprop="name">X</code> &#8212; <span itemprop="purpose">Data sample</span><br/> <span class="add_font_color_general remove_bold"><span class="example_desc"><span itemprop="inputvalue">scalar</span> | <span itemprop="inputvalue">vector</span> | <span itemprop="inputvalue">matrix</span> | <span itemprop="inputvalue">multidimensional array</span></span></span></h3><span class="icon-arrow-open-down icon_24"></span><span class="icon-arrow-open-right icon_24"></span></div><div role="tabpanel" id="expand_panel_body_d120e631073" aria-labelledby="expand_panel_heading_d120e631073" class="panel-collapse collapse in"><div class="panel-body">
                    <p>Data sample, specified as a scalar, vector, matrix, or multidimensional
                        array.</p>
                    <div class="itemizedlist"><ul><li><p>If <code class="argument">X</code> is a scalar, then
                                    <code class="literal">range(X)</code> is 0.</p></li><li><p>If <code class="argument">X</code> is a 0-by-0 empty array, then
                                    <code class="literal">range(X)</code> is also an empty array.</p></li></ul></div>
                <p class="datatypelist"><strong>Data Types: </strong><code itemprop="datatype">single</code> | <code itemprop="datatype">double</code> | <code itemprop="datatype">logical</code> | <code itemprop="datatype">datetime</code> | <code itemprop="datatype">duration</code></p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="panel-group" role="tablist" aria-multiselectable="true"><div class="panel panel-default "><div itemscope="" itemprop="inputargument" itemtype="http://www.mathworks.com/help/schema/MathWorksDocPage/NamedInputArgument" itemid="d120e631141"><div role="tab" data-toggle="collapse" id="expand_panel_heading_d120e631141" data-target="#expand_panel_body_d120e631141" aria-controls="expand_panel_body_d120e631141" class="panel-heading add_cursor_pointer" aria-expanded="true"><span id="inputarg_dim" class="anchor_target"></span><h3 class="panel-title" id="d120e631141"><code itemprop="name">dim</code> &#8212; <span itemprop="purpose">Dimension to operate along</span><br/> <span class="add_font_color_general remove_bold"><span class="example_desc"><span itemprop="inputvalue">positive integer scalar</span></span></span></h3><span class="icon-arrow-open-down icon_24"></span><span class="icon-arrow-open-right icon_24"></span></div><div role="tabpanel" id="expand_panel_body_d120e631141" aria-labelledby="expand_panel_heading_d120e631141" class="panel-collapse collapse in"><div class="panel-body">
                    <p>Dimension to operate along, specified as a positive integer scalar. If you
                        do not specify a value, then the default value is the first array dimension
                        whose size does not equal 1.</p>
                    <p><code class="argument">dim</code> indicates the dimension whose length reduces to
                        1. <code class="literal">size(y,dim)</code> is 1, while the sizes of all other
                        dimensions remain the same unless <code class="literal">size(X,dim)</code> is 0. If
                            <code class="literal">size(X,dim)</code> is 0, then
                            <code class="literal">range(X,dim)</code> returns an empty array of the same size
                        as <a href="#d120e631073" class="intrnllnk"><code class="argument">X</code></a>.</p>
                    <p>Consider a two-dimensional data sample <code class="argument">X</code>:</p>
                    <div class="itemizedlist"><ul><li><p>If <code class="argument">dim</code> is equal to 1, then
                            